{"url": "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics/education/phd-programme", "final_url": "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics/education/phd-programme", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "PhD programme | Utrecht University\nSkip to main content Menu\nSearch uu.nl\nSearch scope\nSubject\nStaff member\nSearch\nSelect language\nNederlands nl\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nResearch\nInstitute for Theoretical Physics\nEducation\nPhD programme\nInstitute for Theoretical Physics\nInstitute for Theoretical Physics\nInstitute for Theoretical Physics\nAbout the ITP Close submenu +\nOrganization\nHistory\nEDI Council\nITP PhD Council\nVacancies\nPartners\nLinks\nIn memoriam \u2013 Umut G\u00fcrsoy\nPeople\nResearch Close submenu +\nCondensed-Matter Theory, Statistical and Computational Physics\nString Theory, Cosmology and Elementary Particles\nEducation Close submenu +\nMaster's programme\nPhD programme\nGerard 't Hooft Fund\nNews & Outreach\nEvents Close submenu +\nSoft Matter and Biophysics Seminar\nNico van Kampen Colloquium\nCosmology Seminar\nCondensed-matter theory seminar\nHydrodynamics in electronic systems\nString Theory Journal Club\nString Theory Seminar Close submenu +\n2025-2026\n2024-2025\n2023-2024\n2022-2023\nOther seminars\nPhD defenses\nAlumni talks\nEvent archives\nContact Close submenu +\nVisitors information\nUU home\nInstitute for Theoretical Physics\nAbout the ITP\nPeople\nResearch\nEducation\nMaster's programme\nPhD programme\nGerard 't Hooft Fund\nNews & Outreach\nEvents\nContact\nPhD programme\nResearch at the Institute for Theoretical Physics (ITP) at Utrecht University covers high-energy physics (elementary particles, quantum gravity, string theory), cosmology (early universe, cosmic microwave background, inflation, gravitational waves), quantum matter (superconductivity, spintronics, Bose-Einstein condensation, quantum Hall effect, quantum computing), and soft matter and biophysics (colloidal self-assembly, iontronics, cell motility, stochastic population dynamics).\nThe institute offers students with an MSc degree the opportunity to enter a four-year\u2019s PhD program in theoretical physics. Apart from their research project PhD students are required to take a number of courses, almost always in the context of the Dutch Research School for Theoretical Physics. They also act as teaching assistants for about ten percent of their working time (usually some form of tutoring in the MSc and BSc physics courses).\nNote that PhD students in the Netherlands in most cases are employed with a salary rather than a stipend, see Obtaining a PhD Position. Openings for PhD positions in the ITP can be found under Vacancies.\nFooter menu (EN)\nGo to\nChoose a programme\nStudent information\nJobs\nAlumni\nGiving\nServices\nIntranet for employees\nCourse planner\nMy Timetable\nAbout UU\nContact\nDirectory\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy\nContact\nFollow UU\nFacebook\nYoutube\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nUtrecht University\nHeidelberglaan 8\n3584 CS Utrecht\nThe Netherlands\nTel. +31 (0)30 253 35 50", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics/education/phd-programme#main-content"], ["", "https://www.uu.nl/en"], ["Nederlands nl", "https://www.uu.nl/onderzoek/instituut-voor-theoretische-fysica"], ["Home", "https://www.uu.nl/en"], ["Research", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research"], ["Institute for Theoretical Physics", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics"], ["Education", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics/education"], ["Institute for Theoretical Physics", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics"], ["Institute for Theoretical Physics", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics"], ["About the ITP", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/institute-for-theoretical-physics/about-us"], ["Organization", "https://www.uu.nl/en/research/in